# Docs, wiki, and screenshots (PR #65)

## What landed

- **Ownership:** install/docs/GHCR URLs use `Shaffer-Softworks/remote-screens` (not `sickkick/…`). Keep `@sickkick` codeowners and `sickkick40@gmail.com` maintainer email. Image: `ghcr.io/shaffer-softworks/remote-screens-{arch}`.
- **GitHub Wiki:** enabled and published at https://github.com/Shaffer-Softworks/remote-screens/wiki (sidebar + Installation, Pairing, Editor, Free-form, Architecture, Demo, Screenshots, Troubleshooting, …). Wiki git remote only exists after the first page is created in the GitHub UI; then push to `remote-screens.wiki.git`.
- **In-repo docs:** `addon/DOCS.md` (Supervisor panel — must stay self-contained), `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `docs/DEMO.md`, `docs/SCREENSHOTS.md`, `docs/TESTING.md`, `docs/REMOTE_COMPOSE.md`. README links the wiki and embeds live screenshots.
- **Screenshots:** under `docs/screenshots/` — `editor-*`, `player-*`, `screens.png`, `themes.png`. No concept mockup JPGs. Wiki embeds via `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Shaffer-Softworks/remote-screens/main/docs/screenshots/<file>.png` (after merge to `main`).

## Capture tooling

- Editor: `node tools/capture_screenshots.mjs http://localhost:18099` (Playwright). Needs demo server; `editor-enroll.png` needs `REMOTE_SCREENS_APK` so `playerApp` is advertised.
- Player: `tools/capture_player_screenshots.sh` against **Pixel_Tablet** (2560×1600 nav tap coords). Prefer Device Manager if CLI emulator dies.
- Demo: `REMOTE_SCREENS_DEMO=1` … see `docs/DEMO.md`. Emulator→host: usually `10.0.2.2:18100`; after wipe with no route, `adb reverse tcp:18100 tcp:18100` and `PLAYER_HOST=127.0.0.1`. Keep the demo server in a long-lived shell (`block_until_ms: 0`) so it is not killed when the agent turn ends.
- Dismiss Android “Viewing full screen / Got it” before final player shots.

## Source split

| Surface | Role |
| ------- | ---- |
| `addon/DOCS.md` | End-user / Supervisor add-on panel |
| GitHub Wiki | Deep browsable guide |
| `docs/*.md` | Maintainer notes (demo, screenshots, testing, Remote Compose) |

Do not add a second GitHub Pages / MkDocs site unless asked.

## Attribution

Never add Cursor as author, co-author, or Made-with trailer. Hooks may inject `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` — strip with `git commit-tree` on the feature branch before the first push (user must approve any force-push after push).

